IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XII -- Shareholders: proposals (s 137).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. Section 137 leans on the regulations
-- throughout ("the prescribed period", "the prescribed number", "the prescribed maximum number of words",
-- "the prescribed minimum amount of support"): each is a plain input, because the regulations are not among
-- the sources. Judgments the section leaves to the corporation ("it clearly appears that ...", "abused to
-- secure publicity") are plain BOOLEAN inputs, and the court's discretion (ss 137(8) and (9)) is never
-- decided: the rule says who may apply and, for (9), the ground the court must be satisfied of.
-- The proposal in s 137 is a notice of a matter a shareholder proposes to raise at an ANNUAL meeting
-- (s 137(1)); the circular is the management proxy circular of s 150 (Part XIII, other module of this piece).
-- Dates: Part XII holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XII -- Shareholders: proposals (s 137)`

§§ `s 137(1) -- the right to submit and to discuss a proposal`

-- (1)(a) A registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting may submit
-- to the corporation notice of a matter they propose to raise at the meeting (a "proposal"), subject to (1.1)
-- (eligibility) and (1.2) (accompanying information). The relation: the shareholder holds the power to submit;
-- the corporation is under the liability to receive it and, by (2), the duty to circulate it.
-- src:1685 | 137 (1) Subject to subsections (1.1) and (1.2), a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares that are entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders may
-- src:1686 | (a) submit to the corporation notice of any matter that the person proposes to raise at the meeting (a “proposal”); and
@ref CBCA s 137(1)(a) (src:1685-1686)
GIVEN `the person is a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible under s 137(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may submit a proposal within s 137(1)(a)` MEANS
        `the person is a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders`
    AND `the person is eligible under s 137(1.1)`

-- (1)(b) The same person may discuss at the meeting any matter on which they would have been entitled to
-- submit a proposal. "Would have been entitled" takes in the (1.1) eligibility, so the one input carries it.
-- src:1685 | 137 (1) Subject to subsections (1.1) and (1.2), a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares that are entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders may
-- src:1686 | (a) submit to the corporation notice of any matter that the person proposes to raise at the meeting (a “proposal”); and
-- src:1687 | (b) discuss at the meeting any matter in respect of which the person would have been entitled to submit a proposal.
@ref CBCA s 137(1)(b) (src:1685-1687)
GIVEN `the person is a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one in respect of which the person would have been entitled to submit a proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may discuss a matter at the meeting within s 137(1)(b)` MEANS
        `the person is a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders`
    AND `the matter is one in respect of which the person would have been entitled to submit a proposal`

§§ `s 137(1.1) -- who is eligible`

-- (a) the person has been, for at least the prescribed period, the registered holder or beneficial owner of at
-- least the prescribed number of outstanding shares; or (b) the person has the support of persons who, together
-- (counting the proposer or not), have been for at least the prescribed period the registered holders or
-- beneficial owners of at least the prescribed number. The two share counts are the shares held or owned for AT
-- LEAST the prescribed period: the caller counts them, so a holding younger than the period is not in the count.
-- src:1689 | (1.1) To be eligible to submit a proposal, a person
-- src:1690 | (a) must be, for at least the prescribed period, the registered holder or the beneficial owner of at least the prescribed number of outstanding shares of the corporation; or
-- src:1691 | (b) must have the support of persons who, in the aggregate, and including or not including the person that submits the proposal, have been, for at least the prescribed period, the registered holders, or the beneficial owners of, at least the prescribed number of outstanding shares of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 137(1.1) (src:1689-1691)
GIVEN `the number of outstanding shares the person has held or owned for at least the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of outstanding shares the person and the persons supporting the proposal have in the aggregate held or owned for at least the prescribed period, the person counted or not` IS A NUMBER
      `the person has the support of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed number of outstanding shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is eligible to submit a proposal within s 137(1.1)` MEANS
        `the number of outstanding shares the person has held or owned for at least the prescribed period` AT LEAST `the prescribed number of outstanding shares`
    OR  (    `the person has the support of those persons`
         AND `the number of outstanding shares the person and the persons supporting the proposal have in the aggregate held or owned for at least the prescribed period, the person counted or not` AT LEAST `the prescribed number of outstanding shares`)

§§ `s 137(1.2), (1.3) -- information that accompanies a proposal, and the word count`

-- (1.2) A proposal must be accompanied by (a) the name and address of the person and, if the person relies on
-- supporters, of the supporters; (b) the number of shares held or owned by the person and, if applicable, by the
-- supporters, and the date the shares were acquired. The text says "paragraph (1)(a)", which is the paragraph
-- that gives the right to submit a proposal: every proposal is in point (finding 1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1693 | (1.2) A proposal submitted under paragraph (1)(a) must be accompanied by the following information:
-- src:1694 | (a) the name and address of the person and of the person’s supporters, if applicable; and
-- src:1695 | (b) the number of shares held or owned by the person and the person’s supporters, if applicable, and the date the shares were acquired.
@ref CBCA s 137(1.2) (src:1693-1695)
GIVEN `the person relies on supporters under s 137(1.1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is accompanied by the name and address of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is accompanied by the name and address of the supporters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares the person holds or owns and the date the shares were acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares the supporters hold or own and the date the shares were acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proposal is accompanied by the information s 137(1.2) requires within s 137(1.2)` MEANS
        `the proposal is accompanied by the name and address of the person`
    AND `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares the person holds or owns and the date the shares were acquired`
    AND (    (NOT `the person relies on supporters under s 137(1.1)(b)`)
         OR  (    `the proposal is accompanied by the name and address of the supporters`
              AND `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares the supporters hold or own and the date the shares were acquired`))

-- (1.3) The (1.2) information is not part of the proposal or of the supporting statement of (3), and is not
-- counted toward the prescribed maximum number of words. So the words that count are the proposal's and the
-- statement's, whatever the length of the (1.2) information; the third input is there to be left out.
-- src:1697 | (1.3) The information provided under subsection (1.2) does not form part of the proposal or of the supporting statement referred to in subsection (3) and is not included for the purposes of the prescribed maximum word limit set out in subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 137(1.3) (src:1697)
GIVEN `the number of words in the proposal` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of words in the supporting statement` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of words in the information provided under s 137(1.2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the words that count toward the prescribed maximum within s 137(1.3)` MEANS
    `the number of words in the proposal` PLUS `the number of words in the supporting statement`

§§ `s 137(1.4) -- proof of eligibility`

-- If the corporation asks for it within the prescribed period, the person who submits a proposal must provide
-- proof, within the prescribed period, that they meet (1.1). The duty arises on a request in time; it is met by
-- proof, given in time, that does show the (1.1) requirements are met. The periods are plain BOOLEANs.
-- src:1699 | (1.4) If requested by the corporation within the prescribed period, a person who submits a proposal must provide proof, within the prescribed period, that the person meets the requirements of subsection (1.1).
@ref CBCA s 137(1.4) (src:1699)
GIVEN `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must provide proof of eligibility within s 137(1.4)` MEANS
    `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period`

@ref CBCA s 137(1.4) (src:1699)
GIVEN `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides proof within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proof shows that the person meets the requirements of s 137(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to provide proof of eligibility is met within s 137(1.4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period`)
    OR  (    `the person provides proof within the prescribed period`
         AND `the proof shows that the person meets the requirements of s 137(1.1)`)

§§ `s 137(5), (5.1) -- exemptions from circulating`

-- (5) A corporation is not required to comply with (2) and (3) if any one of (a) the proposal is not submitted
-- within the prescribed period; (b) it clearly appears the primary purpose is to enforce a personal claim or
-- redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders; (b.1)
-- it clearly appears the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the
-- corporation; (c) not more than the prescribed period before receipt, the person failed to present, in
-- person or by proxy, a proposal that, at the person's request, had been included in a circular for a meeting;
-- (d) substantially the same proposal was submitted to shareholders in a management proxy circular or a
-- dissident's proxy circular for a meeting held not more than the prescribed period before receipt, and did not
-- receive the prescribed minimum amount of support at that meeting; or (e) the rights conferred by the section
-- are being abused to secure publicity. Each is a judgment or a fact the caller supplies.
-- src:1707 | (5) A corporation is not required to comply with subsections (2) and (3) if
-- src:1708 | (a) the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period;
-- src:1709 | (b) it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders;
-- src:1710 | (b.1) it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation;
-- src:1711 | (c) not more than the prescribed period before the receipt of a proposal, a person failed to present, in person or by proxy, at a meeting of shareholders, a proposal that at the person’s request, had been included in a management proxy circular relating to the meeting;
-- src:1712 | (d) substantially the same proposal was submitted to shareholders in a management proxy circular or a dissident’s proxy circular relating to a meeting of shareholders held not more than the prescribed period before the receipt of the proposal and did not receive the prescribed minimum amount of support at the meeting; or
-- src:1713 | (e) the rights conferred by this section are being abused to secure publicity.
@ref CBCA s 137(5) (src:1707-1713)
GIVEN `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not more than the prescribed period before receipt of the proposal, the person failed to present, in person or by proxy, a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at the person's request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantially the same proposal was submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held not more than the prescribed period before receipt and did not receive the prescribed minimum amount of support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) within s 137(5)` MEANS
        `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period`
    OR  `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders`
    OR  `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation`
    OR  `not more than the prescribed period before receipt of the proposal, the person failed to present, in person or by proxy, a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at the person's request`
    OR  `substantially the same proposal was submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held not more than the prescribed period before receipt and did not receive the prescribed minimum amount of support`
    OR  `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity`

-- (5.1) A person who fails to continue to hold or own the (1.1) number of shares up to and including the day of
-- the meeting: the corporation need not set out, in the circular or an attachment, any proposal by that person
-- for any meeting held within the prescribed period after that meeting.
-- src:1715 | (5.1) If a person who submits a proposal fails to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in subsection (1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting, the corporation is not required to set out in the management proxy circular, or attach to it, any proposal submitted by that person for any meeting held within the prescribed period following the date of the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 137(5.1) (src:1715)
GIVEN `the person failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is not required to set out the person's later proposal within s 137(5.1)` MEANS
        `the person failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting`
    AND `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting`

§§ `s 137(2), (3) -- circulating the proposal and the supporting statement`

-- (2) A corporation that solicits proxies shall set out the proposal in the management proxy circular required
-- by s 150 or attach the proposal to it. The duty arises where the corporation solicits proxies and a proposal
-- was submitted by a person who may submit it, and neither exemption applies: the (5) exemptions, and the (5.1)
-- one ("not required to set out"). The relation: the proposer holds the claim; the corporation the duty.
-- src:1701 | (2) A corporation that solicits proxies shall set out the proposal in the management proxy circular required by section 150 or attach the proposal thereto.
@ref CBCA s 137(2) (src:1701)
GIVEN `the corporation solicits proxies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) under s 137(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is not required to set out the proposal under s 137(5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation solicits proxies`
    AND `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it`
    AND (NOT `the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) under s 137(5)`)
    AND (NOT `the corporation is not required to set out the proposal under s 137(5.1)`)

-- The duty is met by setting the proposal out in the circular or attaching it to the circular.
@ref CBCA s 137(2) (src:1701)
GIVEN `the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is set out in the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is attached to the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to circulate the proposal is met within s 137(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)`)
    OR  `the proposal is set out in the management proxy circular`
    OR  `the proposal is attached to the management proxy circular`

-- (3) If the person who submits the proposal so requests, the corporation shall include in the circular, or
-- attach to it, a statement in support of the proposal by the person and the name and address of the person; the
-- statement and the proposal must together not exceed the prescribed maximum number of words. The duty to
-- include arises where the person asks and the (2) duty arises (the (5) exemption is for both (2) and (3)).
-- src:1703 | (3) If so requested by the person who submits a proposal, the corporation shall include in the management proxy circular or attach to it a statement in support of the proposal by the person and the name and address of the person. The statement and the proposal must together not exceed the prescribed maximum number of words.
@ref CBCA s 137(3) (src:1703)
GIVEN `the person who submits the proposal requests a supporting statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must include the supporting statement within s 137(3)` MEANS
        `the person who submits the proposal requests a supporting statement`
    AND `the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)`

@ref CBCA s 137(3) (src:1703)
GIVEN `the corporation must include the supporting statement within s 137(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is included in the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is attached to the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name and address of the person are included or attached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to include the supporting statement is met within s 137(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must include the supporting statement within s 137(3)`)
    OR  (    (    `the statement is included in the management proxy circular`
              OR  `the statement is attached to the management proxy circular`)
         AND `the name and address of the person are included or attached`)

-- The proposal and the statement together must not exceed the prescribed maximum number of words
-- (the words of the (1.2) information are not counted: s 137(1.3)).
@ref CBCA s 137(3) (src:1703)
GIVEN `the words that count toward the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed maximum number of words` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proposal and the statement are within the word limit within s 137(3)` MEANS
    `the words that count toward the prescribed maximum` AT MOST `the prescribed maximum number of words`

§§ `s 137(4) -- nominations for election of directors`

-- A proposal may include nominations for the election of directors if it is signed by one or more holders of
-- shares representing in the aggregate not less than five per cent of the shares, or five per cent of the shares
-- of a class of shares, of the corporation entitled to vote at the meeting at which the proposal is to be
-- presented. The section does not preclude nominations made at a meeting. The signers' fraction is measured
-- over the shares entitled to vote at the meeting, and, for each class, over that class; the caller states them.
-- src:1705 | (4) A proposal may include nominations for the election of directors if the proposal is signed by one or more holders of shares representing in the aggregate not less than five per cent of the shares or five per cent of the shares of a class of shares of the corporation entitled to vote at the meeting to which the proposal is to be presented, but this subsection does not preclude nominations made at a meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 137(4) (src:1705)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`at least five per cent within s 137(4)` x MEANS x AT LEAST (5%)

@ref CBCA s 137(4) (src:1705)
GIVEN `the proposal is signed by one or more holders of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the shares of the corporation entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of each class of shares of the corporation entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proposal may include nominations of directors within s 137(4)` MEANS
        `the proposal is signed by one or more holders of shares`
    AND (    `at least five per cent within s 137(4)` `the fraction of the shares of the corporation entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold`
         OR  any `at least five per cent within s 137(4)` `the fraction of each class of shares of the corporation entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold`)

§§ `s 137(6) -- immunity`

-- No corporation or person acting on its behalf incurs any liability by reason ONLY of circulating a proposal or
-- statement in compliance with the section. The relation: the corporation holds the immunity; the person who
-- would sue is under a disability. A liability on another ground is not touched.
-- src:1717 | (6) No corporation or person acting on its behalf incurs any liability by reason only of circulating a proposal or statement in compliance with this section.
@ref CBCA s 137(6) (src:1717)
GIVEN `the corporation or a person acting on its behalf circulates a proposal or statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circulating is in compliance with s 137` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is claimed by reason only of the circulating` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no liability is incurred by reason only of circulating within s 137(6)` MEANS
        `the corporation or a person acting on its behalf circulates a proposal or statement`
    AND `the circulating is in compliance with s 137`
    AND `the liability is claimed by reason only of the circulating`

§§ `s 137(7) -- notice of refusal`

-- If the corporation refuses to include a proposal in the circular, it shall, within the prescribed period after
-- the day it receives the proposal or (as the case may be) the day it receives the proof of ownership under (1.4),
-- notify the person in writing of its intention to omit the proposal and of the reasons. Which day starts the
-- period is "as the case may be"; the caller folds it into the one input on the period (fork F-137-7).
-- src:1719 | (7) If a corporation refuses to include a proposal in a management proxy circular, the corporation shall, within the prescribed period after the day on which it receives the proposal or the day on which it receives the proof of ownership under subsection (1.4), as the case may be, notify in writing the person submitting the proposal of its intention to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular and of the reasons for the refusal.
@ref CBCA s 137(7) (src:1719)
GIVEN `the corporation refuses to include a proposal in a management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must notify the person of the refusal within s 137(7)` MEANS
    `the corporation refuses to include a proposal in a management proxy circular`

@ref CBCA s 137(7) (src:1719)
GIVEN `the corporation must notify the person of the refusal within s 137(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the intention to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the reasons for the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given within the prescribed period after the day the corporation receives the proposal or, as the case may be, the proof of ownership under s 137(1.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to notify the person of the refusal is met within s 137(7)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must notify the person of the refusal within s 137(7)`)
    OR  (    `the notice is in writing`
         AND `the notice states the intention to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular`
         AND `the notice states the reasons for the refusal`
         AND `the notice is given within the prescribed period after the day the corporation receives the proposal or, as the case may be, the proof of ownership under s 137(1.4)`)

§§ `s 137(8), (9), (10) -- the court, and the Director`

-- (8) On the application of a person submitting a proposal who claims to be aggrieved by the corporation's
-- refusal under (7), a court may restrain the holding of the meeting to which the proposal is sought to be
-- presented and make any further order it thinks fit. The rule says who may apply; the order is the court's
-- discretion and is not decided.
-- src:1721 | (8) On the application of a person submitting a proposal who claims to be aggrieved by a corporation’s refusal under subsection (7), a court may restrain the holding of the meeting to which the proposal is sought to be presented and make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 137(8) (src:1721)
GIVEN `the applicant submitted the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant claims to be aggrieved by the corporation's refusal under s 137(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may apply to the court within s 137(8)` MEANS
        `the applicant submitted the proposal`
    AND `the applicant claims to be aggrieved by the corporation's refusal under s 137(7)`

-- (9) The corporation, or any person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal, may apply to a court for an order
-- permitting the corporation to omit the proposal; the court, if satisfied that (5) applies, may make such order
-- as it thinks fit. Two things are decided: who may apply, and that the court's power to make the order depends
-- on its being satisfied that (5) applies. What order it makes is the court's.
-- src:1723 | (9) The corporation or any person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal may apply to a court for an order permitting the corporation to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular, and the court, if it is satisfied that subsection (5) applies, may make such order as it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 137(9) (src:1723)
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation or an aggrieved person may apply to the court within s 137(9)` MEANS
        `the applicant is the corporation`
    OR  `the applicant is a person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal`

@ref CBCA s 137(9) (src:1723)
GIVEN `an application is made under s 137(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that s 137(5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order on the application within s 137(9)` MEANS
        `an application is made under s 137(9)`
    AND `the court is satisfied that s 137(5) applies`

-- (10) An applicant under (8) or (9) shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is
-- entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
-- src:1725 | (10) An applicant under subsection (8) or (9) shall give the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 137(10) (src:1725)
GIVEN `the applicant applies under s 137(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant applies under s 137(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant must give the Director notice within s 137(10)` MEANS
        `the applicant applies under s 137(8)`
    OR  `the applicant applies under s 137(9)`

@ref CBCA s 137(10) (src:1725)
GIVEN `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 137(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant gave the Director notice of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to give the Director notice is met within s 137(10)` MEANS
        (NOT `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 137(10)`)
    OR  `the applicant gave the Director notice of the application`

@ref CBCA s 137(10) (src:1725)
GIVEN `the application is under s 137(8) or (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 137(10)` MEANS
    `the application is under s 137(8) or (9)`
